<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27391" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lyra</span></b> , ae, f.,
		= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λύρα</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a lute, lyre</i>, a stringed instrument
			resembling the cithara, fabled to have been invented by Mercury and
			presented to Apollo, <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 2, 7</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curvae lyrae parens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 10, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Threiciam digitis increpuisse lyram,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					3, 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mox cecinit laudes prosperiore lyrā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. A.
					A. 3, 50</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 5, 100</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>Lyric poetry, song</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">imbellis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 6, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Aeoliae Lesbis amica lyrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Am. 2, 18, 26</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. P. 3, 3,
			45</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			In gen., <i>poetic genius</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Inferior lyra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 10, 445</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			Lyra, <i>the constellation, the Lyre</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exoriente Lyra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					1, 315</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 3, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr. R.
				R. 2, 5</span></i>.</div>
